From b62d8981a8b9fea3bd0909b6f4543652e1b8a0ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:10:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06902/11362] [outer-loop] bp35: round 7 honest null, notch
 exits ruled out (codex)

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session reproduced the protected L6 notch cleanly
but did not find a safe exit -- ruled out several candidates instead:
ACTION1/ACTION2/ACTION5 are inert at the notch, the consumed second
cyan switch can't be re-clicked, the goal diamond and left blocking
cell don't respond to clicks, and reopening the right shaft's X shield
just converts it back to a pillar hazard.

New mechanic: ACTION7 is a bounded live-play undo (not a no-op) --
repeated presses reversed the two most recent X-toggle changes, with
an undo window that closed after six reversible actions; it appears
usable only before GAME_OVER.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: the saved 194-action
sequence (dict-shaped labels, JSON-normalized before replay) replayed
cleanly from a fresh env.reset() to level=5, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED
-- matches the session's own report, no hidden win, no regression. No
new level banked; frontier stays at level 5. Strongest lead for next
attempt: click the second gravity switch one or two columns earlier,
while still under the x=6/x=7 shields, to avoid the lethal lateral
step from x=5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
